      equipment: 'Xiangqi pieces and optional racks for concealed hand management.',
      dealing: 'Pieces are mixed face down into paired stacks. Players reveal selected bottom pieces to establish priority order, then draft stacks around the layout to form hands (8 pieces each in four-player game).',
    },
    turnFlow: "Priority-order first player leads to trick one; trick winner leads next. Leader plays one valid combination face down and others must play same number of pieces face down. After reveal, highest valid combination of the same type as the lead wins the trick and captures all played pieces. In base Giog, valid lead types are: single, identical pair, Giog noble triple family, Sam Mui (three soldiers/pawns), Si Mui (four soldiers/pawns), and Wu Mui (five soldiers/pawns). A general or marshal cannot be played in first or last trick ('beheading the cock'); violating this voids all captures by that player. For three-piece leads, leader must announce whether the type is Giog or Sam Mui, since only matching type can beat it.",
